1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,804
Not everyone who buys from you has an account.

2
00:00:03,804 --> 00:00:07,848
This video shows how the store keeps guests, how their orders move to

3
00:00:07,848 --> 00:00:11,785
an account when they sign up, how long their personal data is kept,

4
00:00:11,785 --> 00:00:16,530
how to ask your own questions at checkout, and how staff manage their own profile.

5
00:00:21,130 --> 00:00:26,240
Every sale makes a customer record, even when the buyer never signs up.

6
00:00:26,990 --> 00:00:30,607
A guest who signs up later should find their old orders in their

7
00:00:30,607 --> 00:00:34,430
account, but nobody should be able to claim another person's orders.

8
00:00:35,180 --> 00:00:38,191
Personal data should not be kept for ever:

9
00:00:38,191 --> 00:00:43,020
guests' details should expire, and anyone can ask what you hold, or ask

10
00:00:43,020 --> 00:00:44,400
you to erase it.

11
00:00:45,150 --> 00:00:50,330
And some stores need to ask their own questions at checkout, such as a gift message.

12
00:00:54,530 --> 00:00:57,776
Each guest checkout makes its own guest customer.

13
00:00:57,776 --> 00:01:01,730
An email typed at checkout never joins someone else's record.

14
00:01:02,480 --> 00:01:06,703
When a guest creates an account with the same email, and the email

15
00:01:06,703 --> 00:01:12,510
is confirmed, their orders and addresses move to the account, and the guest is marked Merged.

16
00:01:13,260 --> 00:01:17,655
Two settings keep guests' data only as long as you choose, and a

17
00:01:17,655 --> 00:01:19,790
task applies them every day.

18
00:01:20,540 --> 00:01:25,066
Checkout details adds your own fields to the Contact step, and staff have

19
00:01:25,066 --> 00:01:26,900
their own My Account page.

20
00:01:31,087 --> 00:01:33,046
Open Commerce, Customers.

21
00:01:33,046 --> 00:01:36,838
Each guest checkout is its own customer, marked Guest.

22
00:01:36,838 --> 00:01:40,377
A guest who later made an account shows as Merged.

23
00:01:40,830 --> 00:01:42,550
Open the merged guest.

24
00:01:42,550 --> 00:01:47,156
It says the guest's orders and addresses moved to the account, and on

25
00:01:47,156 --> 00:01:50,596
which day, when that account's email was verified.

26
00:01:50,596 --> 00:01:53,360
A merged guest can no longer be edited.

27
00:01:53,813 --> 00:01:59,093
On the account's customer, Orders lists the guest's order, and Merged guest checkouts

28
00:01:59,093 --> 00:02:01,298
lists the guests that joined it.

29
00:02:01,298 --> 00:02:06,520
The Privacy section on each customer, which the Customers and Companies video shows,

30
00:02:06,520 --> 00:02:09,073
has the buttons for a privacy request.

31
00:02:13,275 --> 00:02:15,886
Open Settings, Commerce, Customers.

32
00:02:15,886 --> 00:02:20,597
Erase inactive guests after sets how many months a guest who has not

33
00:02:20,597 --> 00:02:22,444
bought or paid is kept.

34
00:02:22,444 --> 00:02:26,328
After that, the store erases the guest's personal data.

35
00:02:26,328 --> 00:02:28,875
The default is twenty-four months.

36
00:02:29,329 --> 00:02:34,166
Anonymize guest orders after sets how long a paid or canceled guest order

37
00:02:34,166 --> 00:02:38,024
keeps the buyer's name, email, phone and billing address.

38
00:02:38,024 --> 00:02:43,106
After twelve months, by default, they are removed, but the country and region

39
00:02:43,106 --> 00:02:45,066
stay for your tax records.

40
00:02:45,066 --> 00:02:47,148
Enter zero to keep the data.

41
00:02:47,148 --> 00:02:51,189
Customers with an account are kept while the account exists.

42
00:02:51,642 --> 00:02:58,002
On the same page, Billing address at checkout chooses whether buyers must give a billing address.

43
00:03:02,174 --> 00:03:07,307
Some stores need their own questions at checkout, such as a gift message.

44
00:03:07,307 --> 00:03:13,350
With the Checkout details feature on, open Design, Content Types, and Checkout details.

45
00:03:13,350 --> 00:03:15,365
It starts with no fields.

46
00:03:15,365 --> 00:03:16,794
Click Add Field.

47
00:03:17,247 --> 00:03:22,217
Give the field a name, such as Gift message, choose Text Field, and save.

48
00:03:22,670 --> 00:03:26,575
Click Save and Configure, and the field's options open.

49
00:03:26,575 --> 00:03:29,520
Tick Required if buyers must fill it in.

50
00:03:29,520 --> 00:03:33,745
You can add a placeholder, a default value and a length too.

51
00:03:33,745 --> 00:03:34,770
Then save.

52
00:03:38,953 --> 00:03:43,318
On the Contact step of checkout, the buyer now sees the Gift message

53
00:03:43,318 --> 00:03:45,913
field, with the other contact details.

54
00:03:46,368 --> 00:03:50,168
Because it is required, the buyer cannot continue without it.

55
00:03:50,168 --> 00:03:52,833
The buyer types the message, and goes on.

56
00:03:52,833 --> 00:03:56,348
What they typed is kept with the order and the checkout.

57
00:04:00,550 --> 00:04:04,773
Staff have their own page too, under Commerce, My Account, where they edit

58
00:04:04,773 --> 00:04:06,620
how the store addresses them.

59
00:04:10,820 --> 00:04:12,661
A store with many guests:

60
00:04:12,661 --> 00:04:17,590
keep their data for a limited time, and erase it when it is no longer needed.

61
00:04:18,340 --> 00:04:20,043
A shop that sells gifts:

62
00:04:20,043 --> 00:04:23,960
ask for a gift message at checkout, and keep it with the order.

63
00:04:24,710 --> 00:04:26,298
A store for regulars:

64
00:04:26,298 --> 00:04:30,060
guests who sign up find their old orders in their account.

65
00:04:30,810 --> 00:04:32,436
A privacy request:

66
00:04:32,436 --> 00:04:37,720
find the customer, download what you hold, or erase their personal data.

67
00:04:39,720 --> 00:04:47,356
Guests, merged accounts, retention and your own checkout fields keep your customer records useful, and respectful.

68
00:04:47,356 --> 00:04:49,010
Thanks for watching.

